From a9c63e24cb76ef7f16781c0a86b9f9905bad9128 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthieu <59584536+ender9492@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:27:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] block: add fs-blkguard, a boot-chain block-write guard
 (FrameShift)

Refuse writes to boot-chain and unit-unique partitions, identified by
their GPT names as parsed by the kernel, to the whole-disk nodes of the
disks carrying them (sticky per request queue), to SCSI/UFS pass-through,
host-driver SCSI ioctls and partition-table changes; in strict mode
refuse every block device except an allowlist.

Hooks: block device open with FMODE_WRITE, write_iter, fallocate,
BLKDISCARD/BLKSECDISCARD/BLKZEROOUT, BLKROSET clear (single fetch),
BLKPG, BLKRRPART, IOC_PR_*, every write-class bio in
submit_bio_checks(), blk_verify_command() (sd SG_IO,
SCSI_IOCTL_SEND_COMMAND, bsg-scsi), sg write/SG_IO, transport bsg
(UFS BSG), SCSI host-driver ioctls (ufs-qcom UFS_IOCTL_QUERY), START/STOP
UNIT, SG_SCSI_RESET and CDROMEJECT/CLOSETRAY.  Control is
/proc/fs_blkguard: one arming request seals it; the mode never goes
down; strict mode requires kernel.modules_disabled=1.  Boot flag
fs_blkguard=off leaves it unarmed.

No exported symbol, struct layout or Kconfig symbol changes.

Signed-off-by: Matthieu <59584536+ender9492@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
